message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: Proof and replay package for a computer-assisted bound for the de Bruijn-Newman constant
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-29"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23752103
url: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23752103
authors:
  - family-names: Raymond
    given-names: Dale James
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0001-1682-8529
abstract: >-
  Proof and replay materials for the computer-assisted bound
  Lambda <= 427693072077942473661578098491/3961408125713216879677197516800
  < 0.107964910079. The manuscript combines OpenAI's ordinary-zeta theorem
  formalised in Lean, written analytic arguments and exact or directed
  interval computations. Appendix B derives all 67 source chords directly.
  A fifteenth consumer checks their assembly and final functional bindings;
  its prerequisite inequalities remain separately verified obligations.
  This edition supersedes referee edition 3 of 28 October 2026; the numerical plan, source table and comparison history are unchanged; Appendix B adds the direct source reconstruction.
  The release receipt records the actual execution evidence. Component-specific rights are set out in
  LICENSES_AND_RIGHTS.md.
keywords:
  - de Bruijn-Newman constant
  - Riemann zeta function
  - computer-assisted proof
  - heat flow
  - exact arithmetic
  - interval arithmetic
